# No em dashes in content

Do **not** use em dashes (`—`, Unicode U+2014) in user-facing copy:

- UI strings, banners, labels, tooltips, placeholders
- Error and success messages
- Page titles and headings shown to users
- Marketing and help text shipped in the product

**Use instead:**

- Two sentences (period between)
- A comma or colon
- Parentheses
- ` · ` or ` | ` for title separators (e.g. `Compare · Dunedin`, not `Compare — Dunedin`)

**Out of scope:** CSS/code comments and internal design docs unless the task is explicitly to edit that prose.

When touching existing user-facing strings that contain em dashes, replace them as part of the same edit.
